    kg:textSpan "buffer length is over a configurable threshold, the input data pipeline is not the bottleneck. In this case, the Scaler selects a random Pipe with a non- base Variant and scales down its parallelism by a unit (e.g., one process). Importantly, if the current parallelism of cannot be further decreased, cedar will mutate into the base Variant to avoid over-provisioning resources. However, if the output buffer is below a threshold, a bottleneck exists. The Scaler will attempt to scale-up the paralle" .

