    kg:textSpan "remaining samples account for about 20% of the batch size. Note that R t is related to the output length distribution of the model and this experiment is conducted during the early stage of training. As training progresses, R t requires periodic adjustments to adapt to the distribution change. In practice, such changes are usually not too drastic, so the adjustment frequency remains low. and results in fewer micro-batches allocated to each pipeline, thereby partially negating the benefits brough" .

