    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2409_15104_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "PecSched: Preemptive and Efficient Cluster Scheduling for LLM Inference ZEYU ZHANG, University of Virginia, USA HAIYING SHEN, University of Virginia, USA The scaling of transformer-based Large Language Models (LLMs) has significantly expanded their context lengths, enabling applications where inputs exceed 100K tokens. Our analysis of a recent Azure LLM inference trace reveals a highly skewed long-tail distribution of input lengths, with approximately 80% of inputs shorter than 2K tokens. Long i" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2409_15104_rag__chunk_004> a kg:Chunk ;
