    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2501_12407_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "applications. 2 Background We overview key aspects and limitations of the batch and stream processing models ( Table 1 ), including ML data loaders, by analyzing how effectively each system can: Maximize utilization of heterogeneous compute. Manage memory for intermediate data. Minimize overheads for cluster failures and re-scaling. 2.1 Applications We target throughput for ML training and inference pipelines that require data pre- and post-processing using CPUs, GPUs, or both. Similar to curren" .

