    kg:textSpan "mc_val_w_o_sub_w_sub_gpt_4o_mini_56_5=39.9 row: ShareGPT4Video-8B; model_act_net_qa_l_v_bench_per_test_next_qa_vnbench_videomme_test_val_val=50.8; mc_val_w_o_sub_w_sub_gpt_4o_mini_56_5=41.8 row: -; model_act_net_qa_l_v_bench_per_test_next_qa_vnbench_videomme_test_val_val=39.9; mc_val_w_o_sub_w_sub_gpt_4o_mini_56_5=43.6 row: -; model_act_net_qa_l_v_bench_per_test_next_qa_vnbench_videomme_test_val_val=4.5; mc_val_w_o_sub_w_sub_gpt_4o_mini_56_5=47.9 row: -; model_act_net_qa_l_v_bench_per_test_next_" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2507_15507_rag__chunk_002> a kg:Chunk ;
    kg:chunkId "2507.15507_rag::chunk_002" ;
    kg:docId "2507.15507_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2507_15507_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "generally also provide an inconsistent policy gradient estimate. They thus generally do not converge to the optimal policy, even with unlimited available data and unlimited training iterations. We propose a method that corrects for this distribution shift by using importance weighting (IW) ( Shimodaira , 2000 ), called Off-Policy Corrected Reward Modeling (OCRM). While using the resulting corrected RM to estimate each policy gradient would be desirable, obtaining it requires the RM to be retrain" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/2507_19457_rag__chunk_009> a kg:Chunk ;
