    kg:textSpan "(Wu et al., 2025) have successfully adopted this asynchronous paradigm. More specifically, in the asynchronous RL framework, workers continuously stream rollouts generated by the inference engine into a shared buffer, while the training engine independently retrieves rollouts from the buffer for model updates. The disaggregation of the inference and training engines onto distinct groups of computational resources enables fine-grained allocation tailored to task-specific demands. This decoupling " .

