    kg:textSpan "instances, RLBoost then checks if any instance is completely idle (line 21), i.e., is not executing any request. In this scenario, RLBoost finds the most loaded instance with the largest exec (line 22). Different from the scenario with pending requests, migrating executing requests may not lead to earlier completion due to the batching effects of LLMs. If exec is small enough, the generation is completely memory-bound, removing requests from leads to no improvement in inter-token latency (ITL), " .

