    kg:textSpan "as new GPUs become faster. 1. Introduction Whats the limiting factor in faster model training? Hint: it isnt always the GPUs. When training a machine learning model, the life cycle of an individual example spans three stages: reading the example into memory, processing the example in memory, and nally updating model parameters with the example on GPU (e.g. by calculating and then following the gradient). The stage with the lowest throughput determines the overall learning systems throughput. Our" .

