    kg:textSpan "parallelism techniques for long-context inference are fundamentally incompatible with chunked execution . Our work. Medha makes preemptive long-context inference practical by systematically addressing each barrier. We demonstrate that KV-cache read amplification is a non-issue for modern architectures chunks as small as 40 tokens achieve near-optimal efficiency due to high arithmetic intensity in grouped-query attention. We introduce adaptive chunking , which dynamically adjusts chunk sizes as t" .

