    kg:textSpan "we recommend having it at least twice as large as the largest consumer batch, making this share never exceed 50%. We argue that data repetitions are an acceptable tradeoff for flexibility as TensorSocket reduces data movements considerably w/o flexible batching enabled. Repetitions only occur if the consumer batch sizes do not cleanly divide the producer batch size, with Figure 5 depicting a challenging scenario. In practice, we expect the batch sizes requested by consumers to be in powers of tw" .

