    kg:textSpan "Secondly, larger parallelism groups can result in inefficiencies, primarily because of increased communication overhead. Smaller groups tend to perform better. For example, with 512 sequences of 8K, an SP group with a degree > 8 leads to communication time exceeding 31.4% (9.1s) due to the slow inter-node bandwidth. In contrast, groups with a degree of 8 reduce communication to just 7.8% (1.6s), benefiting from the high-bandwidth intra-node connection. In this case, the computation time remains " .

