    kg:textSpan ") accurately. Next, we then analyze the memory consumption and execution time of sequence parallelism with input sequences of variant lengths. Memory consumption has two components: model states and forward activations. Firstly, given a model, in Ulyssesstyle SP, the memory consumption of model states depends only on the ZeRO-stage applied and the number of available devices . For instance, when ZeRO-3 is applied, the model states are evenly sharded over devices, unaffected by SP group selection" .

