    kg:textSpan "when scaling beyond one node (TP size > 8 ). TP balances memory and compute across TP shards, as attention is sharded along the head dimension and all devices process exactly the same data batch ( Shoeybi et al. , 2019 ). quantify how much GPU compute is underutilized due to attention imbalance by measuring the percentage of average idle time to average iteration time; the idle fraction rises to 19% at DP=4 and 55% at DP=8 for a 512K-length workload. In such regimes, variable-length chunking is " .

