    kg:textSpan "GPUs increasing is even more critical to reducing time and economic costs. Traditional parallelisms such as Data Parallelism[ 12 , 37 , 22 , 41 ], Tensor Parallelism[ 37 , 39 , 40 ], and Pipeline Parallelism[ 13 , 10 , 23 , 25 ] distribute the model, input batch, and the optimizer states, but can not directly address the large memory requirement of extremely long sequences as the sequence length dimension remains unchanged. To break through this obstacle, Sequence Parallelism has been introduced" .

