    kg:textSpan ") architectures, conventional layer-level checkpointing offers limited benefits for long sequences due to the static partitioning of the computational graph. Gradient checkpointing applied along the sequence dimension enables maintaining a constant memory footprint for storing forward activations, presenting substantial advantages. Nevertheless, current implementations in mainstream deep learning frameworks ( Chintala et al. , 2016 ; Google , 2015 ) are primarily designed for checkpointing withi" .

