    kg:docId "2408.16978v1_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/2408_16978v1_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "lane contention, latencies of both methods are overpassed by attention computation at around 32k to 64k, and thus, their difference becomes negligible as the sequence length grows larger. Since fetching from one GPU and scattering to other GPUs require additional synchronization and barrier, we choose the first strategy where we allow every GPU to fetch its data without any additional synchronization. Experimental Environment: We use multiple GPU nodes, each with four A100 80 GB, connected via 3" .

