    kg:textSpan "our FPDT-based methods. In this part, we will demonstrate why this is our preference. Figure 12 shows the usage of GPU HBM at different chunk lengths. We conduct the profiling on a single node with 4 GPUs, with a fixed global sequence length of 256K. We change the length of each sequence chunk and compare the corresponding memory footprint and MFU. The chunk size of 256K means that we do not use chunk, but just run the baseline Ulysses. 8K, 16K, 32K, 64K, and 128K of chunk size corresponds to 32" .

