    kg:textSpan "27 ] largely ignore this heterogeneity between short-input and long-input requests. Cluster-level scheduling in current LLM inference systems generally falls into three categories: First-In-First-Out (FIFO) [ 19 , 23 ], reservation-based [ 24 ], and priority-based [ 25 27 ] strategies. However, these works primarily target short-input requests with input lengths below 2K. In clusters with both short-input and long-input requests, FIFO [ 19 , 23 ] can cause head-of-line blocking, where long input" .

