    kg:textSpan "memory optimization during training. In RL training, conservative GPU memory policies are often adopted to prevent OOM: static memory footprints (e.g., optimizer states) are preferentially offloaded to host memory, and parameters and gradients are offloaded when device memory becomes insufficient [ 54 , 56 ]. In addition, as indicated by certain spikes in Figure 23 , the long sequence lengths during training lead to substantial activation footprints [ 20 , 32 ], for which recomputation [ 19 ] is" .

