    kg:textSpan "percentile scheduling time ratio grows approximately linearly. Even when the cluster size reaches 8192 GPUs, the ratio remains below 5.2%, which is acceptable. The scheduling time ratio decreases as model size increases. This is because larger models lead to higher JCTs, while the number of model replicas that influence the scheduling search space becomes smaller, which in turn slightly reduces the scheduling decision time. For example, the scheduling time ratio for Llama-3.1 70B remains below 1" .

